project/kit-appshell-doc-route-flex: anentrypoint-design AppShell .app-main is a FIXED-HEIGHT flex column (.app=100dvh overflow:hidden @media min-width:901px; .app-main height:100% display:flex flex-direction:column overflow-y:auto) built for dashboard panes that fill the viewport. For a LONG-SCROLL DOCUMENT route (marketing/landing) the generic child rule `.app-main > *` MUST carry flex-shrink:0 — without it the default flex-shrink:1 + min-height:0 makes every section collapse to height:0 once content exceeds the container, piling all content on the hero (catastrophic, looks like total layout break). Fixed in app-shell.css line ~333. ALSO mobile (<=480px): the folded .app-chrome>.app-topbar is flex:0 0 auto and sizes to nav content, overflowing the viewport and clipping nav — needs max-width:100%/flex-basis:100%/min-width:0 so the nav overflow-x:auto engages. GENERAL LESSON: DOM overlap/overflow probes do NOT catch height:0 collapse (boxes don't overlap, they're zero) — SCREENSHOT-witness layout, never trust geometry probes alone for 'looks janky' reports. The kit fix (not landing-local CSS) is the proper fix: every AppShell document consumer benefits.